  "annotation": {
    "schema_version": 5,
    "type": "new architecture support",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "The architecture registry lacked DeciLMForCausalLM. The existing Llama builder used uniform attention and MLP dimensions, whereas the new builder consumes per-block attention and feed-forward descriptions.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_24a52f35f1ca4dec876e2c5e69de9c41",
          "call_4982f18891ac4b7bbe4c4303af535a5b",
          "call_5b104c86da754311bb5235e4950819dc"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "Reusing Attention, GatedMLP and TransformerBlock makes this an architecture-composition change rather than a new inference kernel. Per-block construction permits omitted branches and varying widths while retaining existing tensor names and quantization interfaces.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_4982f18891ac4b7bbe4c4303af535a5b",
          "call_836ff0213685478c8f2b5097446530b8",
          "call_aa57b6ead72f49fbb686e925915ab60f"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "Config.from_directory can now select DeciLMConfig, and Model.from_config instantiates its DeciLMModel. Registration does not imply compatibility with every checkpoint advertising that architecture: block_configs is required, and linear-replacement, sparsity and sink-attention options are explicitly rejected for active branches.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_24a52f35f1ca4dec876e2c5e69de9c41",
          "call_7515d5176ffd4cc9a6e3ce71d1853a5c",
          "call_01f09d7d21f0430ea026b1f8cc1e187d",
          "call_4982f18891ac4b7bbe4c4303af535a5b"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "The earlier optional-transformer entry records missing-normalization input handling and empty-block allocation observations.",
        "basis": "ancestor",
        "evidence": [
          "call_eedf8e1f1320496f89ed3e06180f3c34"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The missing-normalization implementation is unchanged, but DeciLM supplies a norm for every active branch, avoiding that trigger. Empty-block allocation still divides by zero when called directly; conversion guards allocate_q with if linears, although its later bitrate calculation has a separate empty-block problem.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_836ff0213685478c8f2b5097446530b8",
          "call_cf2ee5ff3e564600bffda170f26626f0",
          "call_ce7587ef5ac442e7977ecf07afe44277",
          "call_4982f18891ac4b7bbe4c4303af535a5b"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Inspected discussions concern separate issues: #7, \u201cquantizing model: undefined symbol: __cxa_call_terminate,\u201d reports an extension/toolchain problem; #12, \u201cQwen2.5 Coder 0.5B Instruct | ValueError: Unsupported type in stop_conditions,\u201d concerns chat mode; #13 reports conversion without a bos_token_id; #4, \u201cchore: update config.py,\u201d corrects a spelling error. None supplies evidence of DeciLM validation.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_22e03949acd240579a1f24693faa426c",
          "call_5507d772a70b4a00965c79a6d5587616",
          "call_9b8e5dae3daa4d3196676d3412990e74",
          "call_2d67f50df68f47af8387d98706b5cc21",
          "call_507571702b4b4d5283fef62d20e13524"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "No model loading, conversion, tensor inference or GPU execution was performed. Scalar checks reproduce Python dimension arithmetic only.",
      "Configuration compatibility is not tensor-shape or numerical-equivalence validation; checkpoint tensor headers were not inspected.",
      "The code establishes the two-thirds MLP-width transformation and 256-element rounding, but the architectural rationale for those choices is not established by the inspected evidence."
    ],
    "links": [
      "89f6401d65d965d22fbd6d3fece1f5bb8ba8598a"
    ],
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "models",
        "title": "Compose DeciLM blocks from checkpoint configuration",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "DeciLMConfig reads global hidden width, query-head count and normalization epsilon; absent or false-valued head_dim falls back to hidden_size // num_attention_heads. It accepts SiLU or an omitted activation setting, defaults untied embeddings, selects NEOX RoPE layout, and requires one block_configs entry per hidden layer.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_4982f18891ac4b7bbe4c4303af535a5b",
              "call_7515d5176ffd4cc9a6e3ce71d1853a5c"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Each block reads attention and ffn independently. no_op removes that branch and its norm. Active attention maps n_heads_in_group directly to num_kv_heads; Attention uses that value for K/V projection widths and reshaping. Active MLP width is int(2 * ffn_mult * hidden_size / 3), rounded upward to a multiple of 256 using +255 before integer division.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_4982f18891ac4b7bbe4c4303af535a5b",
              "call_aa57b6ead72f49fbb686e925915ab60f"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Checkpoint layer indices remain in tensor keys even when attention is absent. A separate cache_layer_idx advances only for active attention; last_kv_module_idx records the last containing module. This matches Attention's cache.get_layer(layer_idx) access and Model.prefill's stop-at-last-KV behavior.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_4982f18891ac4b7bbe4c4303af535a5b",
              "call_aa57b6ead72f49fbb686e925915ab60f",
              "call_01f09d7d21f0430ea026b1f8cc1e187d"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The model retains embedding \u2192 transformer blocks \u2192 final RMSNorm \u2192 logits Linear ordering. prepare_inputs stores input_ids and delegates attention preparation. The existing helper defaults to uncached Flash Attention, rejects caches for uncached modes, and prepares page tables and sequence lengths for cached Flash Attention.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_4982f18891ac4b7bbe4c4303af535a5b",
              "call_aa57b6ead72f49fbb686e925915ab60f"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The pinned configurations for Deci/DeciCoder-6B, Deci/DeciLM-6b, Deci/DeciLM-6b-instruct, Deci/DeciLM-7B and Deci/DeciLM-7B-instruct use num_key_value_heads_per_layer rather than block_configs. Deci/DeciLM-7B-instruct-GGUF instead declares a global KV-head count and also lacks block_configs. All six share the registered architecture string but do not supply the required new block schema.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_7ace340683e94a2d90915281d9de9c4e",
              "call_5dc21567543d4fe48389a75203f0f274",
              "call_9b451de06fed4950819ab31c952ddfda",
              "call_08149e626dbf4b74b07d0f710430569d",
              "call_3bb25a14eb8f47609862e34d4c4285f5",
              "call_017d5dddfb234053b48ba59ca8768604",
              "call_4982f18891ac4b7bbe4c4303af535a5b"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "nvidia/Llama-3_1-Nemotron-51B-Instruct supplies block_configs, hidden_size 8192 and 64 query heads, but includes active attention with replace_with_linear=true, which the new constructor rejects. Its configuration therefore falls outside the implemented subset.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_81ecfa9c801f46c2b68ea154cfbeb659",
              "call_4982f18891ac4b7bbe4c4303af535a5b"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "nvidia/Llama-3_3-Nemotron-Super-49B-v1 supplies the expected block schema, 8192 hidden width, 64 query heads, eight KV heads on active attention, and attention-only omissions. nvidia/Llama-3_1-Nemotron-Ultra-253B-CPT-v1 and nvidia/Llama-3_1-Nemotron-Ultra-253B-v1 each supply 16384 hidden width, 128 query heads, sixteen KV heads on active attention, and fully omitted blocks as well as attention-only omissions. Each explicitly uses SiLU and untied embeddings; these configuration values fit the builder's corresponding mappings, subject to the empty-block conversion observation.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_60cd332ceddf4de0aeda9b9e6371c468",
              "call_84ab557e901849ac916093bbb60a2210",
              "call_efaf593c692347e58ea3a4fa3ed91195",
              "call_92e12e56cf0c449e985d3687bc303361",
              "call_f8a56c4e21ad43bfb5b61c7f7140bac2",
              "call_4982f18891ac4b7bbe4c4303af535a5b"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A standard-library scalar check yields head_dim=128 for the inspected 4096/32, 8192/64 and 16384/128 configurations. At hidden width 8192, ffn_mult values 0.5, 1 and 5.25 produce widths 2816, 5632 and 28672; at 16384, values 0.4875 and 39 produce 5376 and 425984. These are arithmetic results, not checkpoint or kernel tests.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_53414cc7d7e64d01abab1de1f228189e"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "findings": [
      {
        "id": "empty-block-conversion-bitrate",
        "origin": "authoring_observation",
        "status": "suspected",
        "classification": "defect",
        "description": "The new builder retains fully empty transformer blocks, exposing an unguarded conversion bitrate division.",
        "trigger": "Convert a block with both attention.no_op and ffn.no_op true, as present in both inspected Nemotron Ultra configurations, and reach the post-save bitrate calculation.",
        "expected_behavior": "A parameterless identity block should be skipped or reported without dividing by its weight count.",
        "actual_behavior": "No submodules are registered, so weights_numel() returns zero. Conversion skips allocate_q but subsequently evaluates num_bits / module.weights_numel(), which divides by zero if the preceding save completes.",
        "locations": [
          {
            "commit": "75c7366bb2e2a7671e38d079f9e5f54945b78006",
            "path": "exllamav3/models/decilm.py",
            "symbol": "DeciLMModel.__init__"
          },
          {
            "commit": "29060addb5a3994cec3867e1f2f6b30ecda7b8a3",
            "path": "exllamav3/conversion/convert_model.py",
            "symbol": "main"
          }
        ],
        "source_evidence": [
          "call_4982f18891ac4b7bbe4c4303af535a5b",
          "call_f11f02ec43a0433d9ddb9c5fe019f082",
          "call_ce7587ef5ac442e7977ecf07afe44277",
          "call_84ab557e901849ac916093bbb60a2210",
          "call_92e12e56cf0c449e985d3687bc303361"
        ],
        "verification": [
          {
            "method": "source_inspection",
            "description": "Traced empty-block construction, None-filtering registration and weight summation into conversion. Whole-parent import search located convert.py as the direct CLI entry calling main; this observation concerns conversion, not every inference workflow.",
            "evidence": [
              "call_836ff0213685478c8f2b5097446530b8",
              "call_f11f02ec43a0433d9ddb9c5fe019f082",
              "call_999fa0b2eb5d414cbcbf4978a24d90ee",
              "call_c1092a059fee42fcbbe65ba2697dc4f3",
              "call_ce7587ef5ac442e7977ecf07afe44277"
            ],
            "limits": "No end-to-end conversion or empty-tensor serialization was executed; an earlier failure is not excluded."
          },
          {
            "method": "scalar_transcription",
            "description": "Evaluated the zero-weight division with standard-library Python and observed ZeroDivisionError.",
            "evidence": [
              "call_53414cc7d7e64d01abab1de1f228189e"
            ],
            "limits": "This models the arithmetic only and does not execute the converter."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "summary": "Registers DeciLM and builds heterogeneous Nemotron-style blocks using existing inference modules; older Deci schemas and linear-replacement variants remain outside the implemented subset, and empty blocks expose a conversion hazard."
